<h1>Auto Arrange Labels</h1>
<hr align="left" width="100.526%" size="5" class="whs3">
<p>This command is accessible from <span class="Path" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Labels &gt; Auto Arrange</b></span> in Inspection mode or from the <b style="font-weight:normal;"><span class="Path" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>label context menu</b></span> in <span class="Mode" style="text-decoration:underline;"><u>Edit label</u></span> mode.</b></p>
<p class="Description" style="font-weight:bold;"><b><span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description:</b></span></b></p>
<p class="Description"><b style="font-weight:normal;"><span lang="EN-US">If</span> <span class="Command">Auto Arrange labels</span> <span lang="EN-US">option is enabled, all labels in the report pages will be automatically arranged at the borders of the viewport. Each new label will be placed at the best possible position on the screen. If resize, move or rotate functions are applied to the object, the labels will be automatically rearranged for best correspondence with their connected points.</span></b></p>
<p><b style="font-weight:normal; font-style:normal;"><span lang="EN-US">The command is switched on by default.</span></b></p>
<p class="Note" id="P1"><b style="font-weight:normal;"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Note</b></span><span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>:</b></span> <span lang="EN-US">While the</span> <span class="Command">Auto Arrange Labels</span> <span lang="EN-US">option is active, the labels cant be moved manually to new positions.</span></b></p>
<p>&#160;</p>

